NOTE: BibTeX has no line-comment character. Any line containing an "at" sign
followed by a word starts an entry, so do not paste commented-out examples here
or the build will fail. Plain prose like this, outside of any entry, is ignored.

Add publications as normal BibTeX entries. Beyond the standard fields, al-folio
understands:

  abbr={PRX}            venue badge on the left (style it in _data/venues.yml)
  selected={true}       also surfaced on the homepage
                        (requires selected_papers: true in _pages/about.md)
  bibtex_show={true}    renders a "BibTeX" button
  preview={figure.gif}  thumbnail from assets/img/publication_preview/
  pdf= html= code= poster= slides= arxiv= altmetric= dimensions=
